        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          "Rogue treadmill" is a reasonable thing to search for: Rogue Fitness sells almost everything a garage
          gym needs, and the CrossFit Games run on a Rogue-branded curved treadmill. But Rogue does not design
          or build treadmills. On 5 November 2026 its treadmill category held eight machines from three makers —
          Woodway, TrueForm and STEPR — ranging from $3,495 to $11,395. One of them, the Rogue | Woodway Curve
          LTG, carries Rogue's name; the rest are the makers' own models at, as far as we could check, the
          makers' own prices. This guide lists them all, says what each is for, and covers what buying through
          Rogue changes and what it does not.
